# leakcheck local pattern file — form only, no real identifiers here.
#
# This repository is public (see CLAUDE.md "Public repo — synthetic
# examples only"). scripts/leakcheck.sh greps the tracked tree for internal
# identifiers so they don't leak into a commit. Its pattern list must NOT be
# committed — a denylist of real internal names in a public repo would be
# the leak it exists to prevent — so it lives in .leakcheck.local instead,
# which is gitignored.
#
# To enable the check locally:
#   1. cp .leakcheck.example .leakcheck.local
#   2. Replace the examples below with your own real internal identifiers:
#      internal service/host/queue names, codenames, internal domains, etc.
#
# Format: one extended-regex pattern per line, matched case-insensitively.
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Examples below are synthetic placeholders — delete them and use your own:
# acme-internal-billing-svc
# widget-queue
# [a-z0-9-]+\.acme-corp\.internal
